<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:10:42 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>US-mediated talks on ending Russia-Ukraine war begin in Abu Dhabi</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-us-mediated-talks-on-ending-russia-ukraine-war-begin-in-abu-dhabi</link><description>
Three-way talks between Russia, Ukraine and the US opened Tuesday, November 10, in the United Arab Emirates, as Washington made another push to end the war. The two-day session in Abu Dhabi is the first such meeting since February. It will focus on establishing future security guarantees for the warring countries.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/121a87b4-dd03-11f1-aa06-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-46a35800.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/121a87b4-dd03-11f1-aa06-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-46a35800.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a90e73e-dd01-11f1-891b-45ca0b05ead8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:29:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French students block dozens of schools, vow more protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-french-students-block-dozens-of-schools-vow-more-protests</link><description>
French students blocked the entrances to dozens of high schools on Tuesday, November 10, as they kept up protests for better learning conditions. These protests across France have spiraled into larger cost-of-living demonstrations in recent weeks, some marked by violence and police brutality. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b85f91f0-dd03-11f1-a128-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f6d585f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b85f91f0-dd03-11f1-a128-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f6d585f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1865113a-dd02-11f1-88b2-dd28884026b2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:29:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France vows tough response to freezer cyberattack blamed on Iran</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-france-vows-tough-response-to-freezer-cyberattack-blamed-on-iran</link><description>
France's Foreign Minister Jean-Noel Barrot said Tuesday, November 10, that Paris ruled out "nothing" to respond to a major cyberattack on hundreds of supermarket fridges in October that it has blamed on Iran. The goal, Jean-Noel Barrot told France Info, is "to deter anyone who might be tempted, in Iran or elsewhere, to do it again".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac530400-dcef-11f1-a134-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b0819ef7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac530400-dcef-11f1-a134-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b0819ef7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c512c92e-dcec-11f1-b590-af63ea5b27f6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:51:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Seniors rock the stage: Greek theater seeks to show that 'art has no age'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-seniors-rock-the-stage-greek-theater-seeks-to-show-that-art-has-no-age</link><description>
A recent Greek National Opera production afforded a group of seniors the chance to channel their young-at-heart energy into onstage performances, proving that no one's too old to learn something new. It challenged the premise that retirement means surrendering to a sedentary lifestyle and extinguishing one’s creative spirit.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4943225e-dcf0-11f1-a4a2-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-39b7fb4b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4943225e-dcf0-11f1-a4a2-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-39b7fb4b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fca458f6-dcee-11f1-a199-a73f6fca2e5d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:50:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia and Ukraine hold US-backed talks after Trump says broad deal is possible</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-russia-and-ukraine-hold-us-backed-talks-after-trump-says-broad-deal-is-possible</link><description>
Russian and Ukrainian officials met on Tuesday, November 10, for their first US-brokered talks since February, after US President Donald Trump suggested last week that a broad deal was possible on ending the war in Ukraine and guaranteeing security in Europe. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv Emmanuelle Chaze and FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Rochelle Ferguson have more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33b5a36a-dcf2-11f1-83f9-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3925831b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33b5a36a-dcf2-11f1-83f9-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3925831b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb9f108e-dcea-11f1-afa5-019a9f7fc105</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:40:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Rubio hails 'very productive' Ukraine-Russia talks, calls to include Europeans</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-live-ukraine-russia-and-us-to-resume-peace-talks-in-abu-dhabi</link><description>
Negotiators from Ukraine, Russia and the United States met for their first trilateral talks in more than nine months in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday, as Washington seeks to broker an end to the war and Kyiv faces pressure over territorial concessions. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio hailed the talks as "very productive" and said the discussions should be expanded to include Europeans at the table. Follow our live blog for the latest developments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f4e976a-dd10-11f1-9ed6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314354614659.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f4e976a-dd10-11f1-9ed6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314354614659.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b1097d2e-dcba-11f1-a827-7bad94ce420d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:09:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f4e976a-dd10-11f1-9ed6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314354614659.jpg">© Altaf Qadri, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK writer M. John Harrison wins Booker Prize for AI-tinged apocalyptic novel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-uk-writer-m-john-harrison-wins-booker-prize-for-ai-tinged-apocalyptic-novel</link><description>
UK author M. John Harrison won the Booker Prize on Monday for his enigmatic novel "The End of Everything", which echoes concerns about artificial intelligence in a darkly satirical depiction of post-apocalyptic Britain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a8ae5c2-dc8a-11f1-aa1e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/b494e954a69a687575dd83c9c41ab832139bc0fd.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a8ae5c2-dc8a-11f1-aa1e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/b494e954a69a687575dd83c9c41ab832139bc0fd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4bbbc5a6-dc8a-11f1-8036-c3ccd3b6a869</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 22:09:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a8ae5c2-dc8a-11f1-aa1e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/b494e954a69a687575dd83c9c41ab832139bc0fd.jpg">© Justin Tallis, AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>What to expect as Russia, Ukraine and the US hold trilateral talks in Abu Dhabi</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-what-to-expect-as-russia-ukraine-and-us-hold-trilateral-talks-in-abu-dhabi</link><description>
Negotiators from Ukraine, Russia and the United States are set to meet in the capital of the United Arab Emirates (UAE) on Tuesday for a new round of talks aimed at ending nearly five years of full-scale war triggered by Moscow's invasion of its neighbour. Security guarantees for the warring sides are set to top the agenda, with US officials insisting that a broader security architecture for Europe must be part of any peace deal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e77aaca-dc82-11f1-9693-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T090059Z-1254041086-RC26DNA29012-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-USA-RUSSIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e77aaca-dc82-11f1-9693-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T090059Z-1254041086-RC26DNA29012-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-USA-RUSSIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82ede6be-dc6f-11f1-b66f-c9c2e19e7715</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 21:46:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e77aaca-dc82-11f1-9693-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T090059Z-1254041086-RC26DNA29012-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-USA-RUSSIA.jpg">© Gavriil Grigorov, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Paris prosecutor opens probe into IRGC cyber unit Shahid Kaveh over fridge cyberattacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/paris-prosecutor-opens-probe-into-irgc-cyber-unit-shahid-kaveh-over-fridge-cyberattacks</link><description>
The Paris prosecutor said she had opened an investigation into Shahid Kaveh, a shadowy cyber unit of the IRGC, the Islamic republic's ideological army, over the 'unprecedented' cyberattacks targeting French supermarkets' fridges in October. Little is known about the Shahid Kaveh unit, although analysts have long observed that the IRGC, which has a vast network of operations, had actively branched out into cyber warfare in recent years. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/93dd0826-dc77-11f1-8ea8-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-203104-203701-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/93dd0826-dc77-11f1-8ea8-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-203104-203701-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">98bdc0ec-dc77-11f1-813e-1967698c37ee</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 20:06:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Sexual predator' Russell Brand jailed for 10 years for rape, assault</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault</link><description>
British comedian and TV star Russell Brand was Monday jailed for more than 10 years for a string of sex offences including rape, as the judge told him he had been a "sexual predator" whose fame had protected him. Brand, 51, showed no emotion as judge Joel Bennathan said he had acted with "staggering arrogance" and shown "contempt" for his victims, who had suffered significant and lasting harm. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6830bca-dc76-11f1-ad17-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-201213-201409-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6830bca-dc76-11f1-ad17-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-201213-201409-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc339a6c-dc76-11f1-a4b3-a141c2237e68</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 20:03:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French PM brings forward hike in minimum wage to calm protesters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-brings-forward-hike-in-minimum-wage-to-calm-protesters</link><description>
French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said ​on Monday, November 9, he was bringing forward a planned hike in the minimum wage to December from January, as he sought to defuse a cost-of-living crisis that has sparked some of France's worst civil unrest in years. Unions swiftly dismissed the offer as "crumbs".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/068341e0-dc5c-11f1-bfb5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5c68cb31.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/068341e0-dc5c-11f1-bfb5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5c68cb31.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b69f81e4-dc5a-11f1-b0d2-d9856f8454a6</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 16:47:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>France accuses Iran of hacking supermarket fridges</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-iran-revolutionary-guards-behind-cyberattacks-on-supermarket-fridges-says-french-fm-barrot</link><description>
French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot on Monday accused Iran's Revolutionary Guards of being behind a recent cyberattack on French supermarket fridges, saying there would be consequences for the country. The Paris prosecutor's office said it had opened an investigation into an Iranian cyber unit affiliated with the Guards over the cyberattacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e20f87a-dc60-11f1-bd65-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3247KH-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e20f87a-dc60-11f1-bd65-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3247KH-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ecd686ae-dc5a-11f1-99f4-e15886b57e2b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 16:42:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e20f87a-dc60-11f1-bd65-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3247KH-2.jpg">© Fred Tanneau, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Sexual predator' Russell Brand jailed for 10 years for rape, assault</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault</link><description>
British comedian and TV star Russell Brand was Monday jailed for more than 10 years for a string of sex offences including rape as the judge told him he had been a "sexual predator" whose fame had protected him.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dcb92508-dc58-11f1-a31f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3-4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dcb92508-dc58-11f1-a31f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3-4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fafd46ca-dc58-11f1-abd1-f3ac760b683e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 16:16:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Spain's right holds poll lead over Sanchez's Socialists ahead of November 29 snap election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-spain-right-leads-sanchez-socialists-in-polls-for-november-29-snap-election</link><description>
Spain's ruling Socialists have narrowed the gap but continue to trail the conservative People's Party, who would need to team up with the far-right Vox party to secure a majority of seats in parliament, pollsters say with three weeks to go before the country's general election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/153b7c44-dc51-11f1-802b-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26309609950350.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/153b7c44-dc51-11f1-802b-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26309609950350.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a445d4a-dc4d-11f1-8d39-35bed1941b1f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 15:46:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/153b7c44-dc51-11f1-802b-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26309609950350.jpg">© Francisco Seco, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Shock and grief in Poland after weekend mass shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-shock-and-grief-in-poland-after-weekend-mass-shooting</link><description>
Poland was in shock after a weekend mass shooting in which a gunman opened fire, killing six people and wounding 15 in the city of Krakow before police shot and wounded him. The shooter died in the hospital on Monday morning, police said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/62896c8a-dc4d-11f1-a7cd-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/62896c8a-dc4d-11f1-a7cd-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">978298e4-dc4d-11f1-baf1-0f4bf4eeecfe</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 15:31:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russell Brand sentenced to 10 years, 6 months for rape and sexual assault</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-russell-brand-sentenced-to-10-years-6-months-for-rape-and-sexual-assault</link><description>
Comedian Russell ​Brand, once one ‌of Britain's most high-profile broadcasters, ⁠was sentenced to 10-and-a-half years in prison on Monday after he was convicted of raping one woman and ‌sexually assaulting three more around two decades ago.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53ca4e84-d924-11f1-a998-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6FC68G.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53ca4e84-d924-11f1-a998-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6FC68G.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">960e6b3e-dc4b-11f1-8597-ff89e763d82b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 14:45:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53ca4e84-d924-11f1-a998-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6FC68G.jpg">© Henry Nicholls, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Saving the Venetian lagoon: A natural buffer against climate change</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261109-saving-the-venetian-lagoon-a-natural-buffer-against-climate-change</link><description>
The Venetian lagoon is home to "barene" – salt marshes made of vegetation and mud, which play an important role against the effects of climate breakdown. They absorb CO2 and can store it long term in the soil, even more efficiently than land forests. But erosion and rising sea levels are threatening these natural ramparts. Today, scientists and environmental associations are trying to save these unique ecosystems. Our Italy correspondent Natalia Mendoza reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b69455a-da01-11f1-826d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-ITALIE-LAGINE-DE-VENISE-BAIN-Lauren-transfer.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b69455a-da01-11f1-826d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-ITALIE-LAGINE-DE-VENISE-BAIN-Lauren-transfer.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b34a085c-da02-11f1-baf2-256ac700330e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 14:18:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Natalia MENDOZA</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>COP31: A focus on electrification as extreme weather events shake the world</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-cop31-a-focus-on-electrification-as-extreme-weather-events-shake-the-world</link><description>
Most of the world’s countries are gathering this week for COP31 in Antalya, Turkey. This United Nations Climate Change Conference opens amid deep concern following extreme weather events such as the deadly floods in Nepal and a supersized El Niño. Experts say that in uncertain times, it is even more important to accelerate global efforts.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/76c8aad8-dc40-11f1-a1b6-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6ef24e83.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/76c8aad8-dc40-11f1-a1b6-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6ef24e83.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec566b74-dc3f-11f1-a1af-414fb17c02dd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 13:35:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French policemen go on trial over 2020 beating of Black music producer</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-policemen-go-on-trial-over-2020-beating-of-black-music-producer</link><description>
Three French policemen went on trial on Monday, November 9, over the beating of a Black music producer they say was not wearing a face mask during the Covid pandemic, in a rare police brutality case to go to court. The assault on Michel Zecler, now 47, triggered renewed outrage in France over police violence, which victims and researchers say is systemic.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cafdf154-dc30-11f1-ab7d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-65c391f2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cafdf154-dc30-11f1-ab7d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-65c391f2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">047c8fea-dc30-11f1-9f34-cb2aca4f3d25</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 11:38:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French PM Lecornu holds talks over protesters' cost-of-living concerns</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-lecornu-holds-talks-over-protesters-cost-of-living-concerns</link><description>
French Prime ⁠Minister Sebastien Lecornu is set to meet ​representatives of employers' organisations and private-sector unions on Monday, November 9, to try ​to address cost-of-living concerns that have sparked some of France's worst civil unrest in years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78db7dc4-dc26-11f1-b24f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-225c2d56.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78db7dc4-dc26-11f1-b24f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-225c2d56.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dff82a58-dc25-11f1-84f0-7f093a5bc218</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 10:40:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Poland begins 2 days of national mourning after gunman kills 6</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-poland-begins-2-days-of-national-mourning-after-gunman-kills-6</link><description>
Poland has begun two days of national mourning after a gunman opened fire in Krakow's main square Saturday afternoon, November 7. Six people were killed and at least 15 were injured. The gunman was shot and detained by police. He then died later in hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a6db9f8-dc23-11f1-b512-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-073e83b4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a6db9f8-dc23-11f1-b512-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-073e83b4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">13df69ca-dc22-11f1-ab91-8931e64b7177</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 10:37:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>European troops in Poland: 'Coalition of the Willing' holds military exercises</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-european-troops-in-poland-coalition-of-the-willing-holds-military-exercises</link><description>
Some 2,800 troops from 10 different European countries are taking part in a multinational military exercise in Poland.  The aim is to prepare European forces for a possible deployment to Ukraine after hostilities end.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea7c605c-dc20-11f1-830c-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8c8ef9be.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea7c605c-dc20-11f1-830c-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8c8ef9be.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9cf6136a-dc1f-11f1-b4af-1b5cf7826bec</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 09:53:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Nazi vanity project': Eagle's Nest in Bavarian Alps a symbol of regime's 'conquest of nature'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nazi-vanity-project-eagle-s-nest-in-bavarian-alps-a-symbol-of-regime-s-conquest-of-nature</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Sir Richard Evans, British Historian and Regius Professor Emeritus of History at the University of Cambridge. The controversy surrounding the fate of Adolf Hitler's Eagle's Nest, the Nazi-era mountaintop complex in the Bavarian Alps, raises profound questions about the relationship between architecture, historical memory and political extremism. At the heart of the debate lies a difficult distinction: preserving the material evidence of history is not necessarily the same as preserving the symbols through which a criminal regime sought to glorify itself. "This is a Nazi vanity project," Evans argues and his conclusion is unequivocal: the mountain must be "restored to its natural state."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/72f70d2c-dc1e-11f1-be8f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-081027-081758-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/72f70d2c-dc1e-11f1-be8f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-081027-081758-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">783f4a56-dc1e-11f1-8f8e-1fe61d6ccdf1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 09:45:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'We call it war-life balance': Daryna's daily struggle to live, survive in wartime Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-we-call-it-war-life-balance-daryna-s-daily-struggle-to-live-survive-in-wartime-ukraine</link><description>
Daryna, 25, entered adulthood in a country at war. Since Russia’s full-scale invasion, her days have been shaped by air raid alerts, power outages and nights spent sheltering in the subway. Despite the uncertainty that shadows every day, she is determined to preserve a semblance of normal life in Kyiv. FRANCE 24 met a young woman who has become emblematic of a generation learning to live under daily bombardment.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2684a786-d8fb-11f1-b43f-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/vlcsnap-2026-11-04-17h06m33s709.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2684a786-d8fb-11f1-b43f-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/vlcsnap-2026-11-04-17h06m33s709.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf10e748-db85-11f1-a1a0-950dde43bd59</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 09:10:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2684a786-d8fb-11f1-b43f-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/vlcsnap-2026-11-04-17h06m33s709.png">© Melina Huet, FRANCE 24</source><dc:creator>Assiya HAMZA</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Poland braces for tense week after deadly Krakow shooting deepens political divisions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-poland-braces-for-tense-week-after-deadly-shooting-deepens-political-divisions</link><description>
Poland faces a week of political tensions after its deadliest shooting in decades left six people dead and dozens wounded in Krakow on Saturday. The attack has heightened concerns over rising far-right extremism ahead of a major nationalist march.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f756ea2-dc0d-11f1-8fe8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6UZ7WF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f756ea2-dc0d-11f1-8fe8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6UZ7WF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">49951798-dc10-11f1-8540-695d250e4c61</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 07:43:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f756ea2-dc0d-11f1-8fe8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6UZ7WF.jpg">© Wojtek Radwanski, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>The week in pictures: US midterms 'Blue Wave', French protests and Dakar Youth Olympics</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-the-week-in-pictures-trump-midterms-debacle-french-protests-dakar-youth-olympics</link><description>
From the Democratic Party's big wins in the US midterm elections to France's ongoing student-led protests and the first Olympic sports event held on African soil, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the week's most striking images.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b6cb3870-db7e-11f1-a1cc-330d38f8a0f8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:21:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg">© Kieran Cleeves, OIS/IOC via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Poland in shock after 6 killed in Krakow far-right shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/poland-in-shock-after-6-killed-in-krakow-far-right-shooting</link><description>
Poland on Sunday launched a terror probe into the mass shooting in Krakow the day before, in which six people were killed and many more were injured. Authorities have said that the 24-year-old suspect, who used a semi-automatic rifle in his killing spree, was “fascinated by far-right ideologies”. He is currently in critical condition in hospital. FRANCE 24 journalist Adrien Sariat reports from Poland.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cea55f2-db7e-11f1-bd0a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150134-150232-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cea55f2-db7e-11f1-bd0a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150134-150232-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">620ad868-db7e-11f1-9f57-c1ea51b6f7a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:21:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mourning in Poland after mass shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/mourning-in-poland-after-mass-shooting</link><description>
Poland has launched a terrorism investigation after a deadly shooting left six people dead and 16 injured. The 24-year-old Polish suspect was reportedly fascinated by far-right ideologies. Authorities are investigating the possible extremist motive as Krakow's main square remains sealed. Two days of national mourning have been declared for the victims.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac245178-db7d-11f1-9478-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140118-140318-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac245178-db7d-11f1-9478-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140118-140318-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b127f486-db7d-11f1-8be9-85907240b2be</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:18:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Europe will take part in US-mediated Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi, French FM says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-europe-will-take-part-us-mediated-ukraine-peace-talks-abu-dhabi-french-fm-says</link><description>
France will participate in the upcoming Abu Dhabi peace talks on ending the Ukraine war, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said Sunday, adding that Europeans will be represented at the summit. The talks will take place under US mediation on Tuesday and Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d3784e-db7b-11f1-a752-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T022255Z-1628715710-RC2ZDOAFTXRB-RTRMADP-3-G20-MINISTERS-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d3784e-db7b-11f1-a752-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T022255Z-1628715710-RC2ZDOAFTXRB-RTRMADP-3-G20-MINISTERS-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3ba58f6-db7a-11f1-9002-631a5aa7e06e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:16:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d3784e-db7b-11f1-a752-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T022255Z-1628715710-RC2ZDOAFTXRB-RTRMADP-3-G20-MINISTERS-1.jpg">© Megan Varner, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Poland launches terrorism probe into mass shooting in Krakow</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-poland-launches-terrorism-probe-into-krakow-mass-shooting</link><description>
Poland on Sunday launched a terror probe into the mass shooting in Krakow the day before, in which six people were killed and many more were injured. Authorities have said that the 24-year-old suspect, who used a semi-automatic rifle in his killing spree, was “fascinated by far-right ideologies” and died in hospital on Monday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1250eae-db5d-11f1-9d08-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/df1b226879aa9026b8f83a806b14523cef6d3728.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1250eae-db5d-11f1-9d08-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/df1b226879aa9026b8f83a806b14523cef6d3728.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c557d2b2-db52-11f1-9660-1f24a097f366</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 08:59:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1250eae-db5d-11f1-9d08-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/df1b226879aa9026b8f83a806b14523cef6d3728.jpg">© Wojtek Radwanski, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
